      "abstractNote": "This software repository provides an approach for exploring and evaluating literature-based document-to-document (doc-2-doc) recommendations using the Word2Vec technique. The methodology generates document-level embeddings by aggregating word embeddings into centroids. It utilizes the RELISH Corpus, a biomedical literature dataset curated by experts, containing pairwise document assessments.\n\nThe software workflow includes training Word2Vec models on a predefined training set, followed by the evaluation of doc-2-doc recommendations using a distinct test set. Additionally, Optuna is integrated for hyperparameter optimization of the trained Word2Vec models using the validation dataset, enabling fine-tuning of model performance.",
