          "lastName": "Castro"
        }
      ],
      "abstractNote": "This release contains the Docker container for the OntoClue project, designed to facilitate reproducible and efficient document-to-document similarity assessments using the RELISH Corpus.\n\nAbout OntoClue\n\nOntoClue is a project focused on evaluating document-to-document similarity through various embedding techniques. The project leverages the RELISH Corpus, a curated resource for benchmarking document similarity within biomedical literature. The RELISH Corpus consists of PubMed IDs (PMIDs) paired with expert-curated relevance assessments, classifying document pairs as relevant, partial, or irrelevant.\n\nThe OntoClue project explores multiple approaches, each accompanied by detailed explanations and documentation. These approaches are implemented in separate repositories, and users can run them individually according to the instructions provided.\n\nDockerized Version of OntoClue\n\nThis Docker container version of OntoClue ensures consistency and reproducibility across experiments, allowing users to train and evaluate neural network models on the RELISH Corpus with ease. The container streamlines the entire workflow, which includes the following steps:\n\n\n\nCloning the relevant repository: Each selected approach's repository is cloned, containing all the necessary code and configurations.\n\nDownloading pre-processed datasets: Based on the chosen approach (e.g., normal text vs annotated text), the appropriate datasets are automatically downloaded.\n\nRunning integrity tests: The pipeline includes tests to verify the integrity of the dataset and ensure the reproducibility of results.\n\nEvaluating models: Once the setup is complete, the models are evaluated to assess document-to-document similarity using the RELISH Corpus.\n\n\nWith this Docker container, users can execute the entire pipeline with a few simple commands, ensuring consistent results for document similarity assessments in biomedical literature.",
